-- the branches of a split are checked against goals of their own, so implicit arguments found in
-- one hold whatever the others hold: an elaboration in a branch does not stop the rest, and the
-- solutions of every branch are returned together (one recheck for a split of many branches, not
-- one per branch)
and-br r k = case r of ok → k; elab ds → (case k of elab ds2 → elab (lapp ds ds2); _ → elab ds); _ → r
